@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 47A — "ניכוי בשל תשלומי ביטוח לאומי ומס מקביל". Row IL-27. Source lines 1791-1797.
--
-- (a) An individual who paid in a tax year National Insurance contributions, and parallel tax, on income that is not work income, deducts
-- 52% of what he paid, excluding the addition under s 179(a) of the National Insurance Law, but not more than his taxable income before the
-- deduction. (b) The same for an individual whose employer is not liable to pay for him and who is liable on his work income. (b1) (from tax
-- year 2025) An individual who received in a year a refund of contributions overpaid in an earlier year deducts 52% of the contributions
-- paid in the year less the refund; if the refund exceeds the contributions paid, 52% of the difference is business income of the year.
-- (c) medical insurance for a person exempt from parallel tax, up to the parallel tax that would have applied. (d) The provisions of the
-- section concerning the Parallel Tax Law apply only for the period ending on 31 December 1996.
--
-- THE PARALLEL TAX LAW applies to no tax year from 1997, so for the tax years this row answers (from 2024) there is no parallel tax to deduct
-- and (a) and (b) are about the National Insurance contributions alone. The National Insurance Law is not encoded here: the contributions paid
-- (net of the s 179(a) addition) are inputs.
-- (b1) applies to tax years from 2025: for 2024 the refund is not looked at.
-- FORK F9a: whether (a)'s cap on taxable income survives (b1)'s "notwithstanding (a)". FORK F9: whether (c) survives (d). Each RULED by Meng on
-- 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default declined where the readings give different answers.
-- (c) names a body "שקבע שר האוצר" (regulations of 5751-1991, not in the source bundle).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 47A — National Insurance contributions`

-- src:1792 | (א) יחיד שבשנת מס שילם דמי ביטוח לפי חוק הביטוח הלאומי [נוסח משולב], התשכ״ח–1968 (להלן – חוק הביטוח), ומס מקביל לפי חוק מס מקביל, התשל״ג–1973 (להלן – מס מקביל), בשל הכנסה שאינה הכנסת עבודה, יותר לו ניכוי של 52% מהסכום ששילם, למעט תוספת לפי סעיף 179(א) לחוק הביטוח, ובלבד שהניכוי לא יעלה על הכנסתו החייבת שלפני הניכוי.
-- src:1793 | (ב) הוראות סעיף קטן (א) יחולו גם לגבי יחיד שמעבידו אינו חייב בתשלום מס מקביל בעדו או בתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי בעדו והוא חייב בתשלומם לגבי הכנסת העבודה שלו.
-- src:1794 | (ב1) [note: (יחול על בירור הכנסתו החייבת של יחיד החל משנת המס 2025 ואילך):] על אף האמור בסעיפים קטנים (א) ו־(ב), קיבל יחיד בשנת מס מסוימת החזר מהמוסד לביטוח לאומי בשל תשלום ביתר של דמי ביטוח ששילם בשנת מס קודמת, כאמור בסעיף 362 לחוק הביטוח (בסעיף קטן זה – החזר), יותר לו ניכוי של 52% מסכום דמי הביטוח ששילם בשנת המס המסוימת לאחר שהופחת מהם סכום ההחזר שקיבל באותה השנה; עלה סכום ההחזר שקיבל יחיד בשנת מס מסוימת על סכום דמי הביטוח ששילם באותה שנת מס, יראו 52% מההפרש, לעניין פקודה זו, כהשתכרות או כרווח מעסק או ממשלח יד של מי שקיבל אותם, בעת שקיבל אותם; לעניין זה, ”סכום ההחזר“ – למעט תוספת ששולמה לפי סעיף 362 לחוק הביטוח.
-- src:1795 | (ג) יחיד שמעבידו אינו חייב בתשלום מס מקביל בעדו וגם הוא עצמו אינו חייב בתשלום מס מקביל, וכן יחיד אחר הפטור מתשלום מס מקביל, יותר לו ניכוי של 52% מהסכומים ששילם בעד ביטוח רפואי שאינו ביטוח רפואת שיניים, לגוף שקבע שר האוצר לאחר התייעצות עם שר הבריאות, עד לסכום המס המקביל שהיה חל לגביו אילו היה חייב בתשלומו.
-- src:1796 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (קביעת גופים לענין סעיף 47א), התשנ״א–1991.]
-- src:1797 | (ד) הוראות סעיף זה לענין חוק מס מקביל יחולו רק בעד התקופה המסתיימת ביום כ״א בטבת התשנ״ז (31 בדצמבר 1996).

@ref ITO s 47A(b1), line 1794; fork F9a
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 47A(b1) does not say whether the cap of subsection (a) on the deduction survives it, and here the cap decides` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 47A(b1) does not say whether the cap of subsection (a) on the deduction survives it, and here the cap decides"

@ref ITO s 47A(c), (d), lines 1795, 1797; fork F9
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 47A(c) does not say whether it survives subsection (d) for a tax year after 1996, and here medical insurance sums were paid` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 47A(c) does not say whether it survives subsection (d) for a tax year after 1996, and here medical insurance sums were paid"

@ref ITO s 47A(c), line 1795: the cap is the parallel tax that would have applied, and there is none after 1996
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 47A(c) caps the deduction at the parallel tax that would have applied, and the Parallel Tax Law applies to no tax year after 1996, so the text gives no cap` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 47A(c) caps the deduction at the parallel tax that would have applied, and the Parallel Tax Law applies to no tax year after 1996, so the text gives no cap"

@ref ITO s 47A(b1), line 1794; fork F9a; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the cap of section 47A(a) in subsection (b1)`
`section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of the cap in subsection (b1)` MEANS
    `declined where the cap decides`

@ref ITO s 47A(c), (d); fork F9; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 47A(c) after 1996`
`section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of subsection (c)` MEANS
    `declined where medical insurance sums were paid`

-- (a), (b): the contributions on which the deduction is given: those paid on income that is not work income, and on work income by one whose
-- employer is not liable, less the addition under s 179(a) of the National Insurance Law that they include.
@ref ITO s 47A(a), (b), lines 1792-1793
GIVEN c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47A — the contributions paid, less the s 179(a) addition, for` c MEANS
    max 0 (c's `contributions paid in the tax year on income that is not work income`
           PLUS c's `contributions paid in the tax year on work income, his employer not being liable to pay for him`
           MINUS c's `additions under section 179(a) of the National Insurance Law included in those contributions`)

-- The deduction of (a), (b) and (b1), without the cap, and the refund that exceeds the contributions.
@ref ITO s 47A(a), (b), (b1), lines 1792-1794
GIVEN c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47A — the deduction before any cap, for` c MEANS
    IF   `the refund counts`
    THEN 52% TIMES max 0 (`s 47A — the contributions paid, less the s 179(a) addition, for` c MINUS c's `refund received in the tax year of contributions overpaid in an earlier year, without any addition under section 362`)
    ELSE 52% TIMES `s 47A — the contributions paid, less the s 179(a) addition, for` c
    WHERE `the refund counts` MEANS c's `tax year` AT LEAST 2025 AND c's `refund received in the tax year of contributions overpaid in an earlier year, without any addition under section 362` GREATER THAN 0

-- (b1): 52% of the difference by which the refund exceeds the contributions paid in the year is business income of the year.
@ref ITO s 47A(b1), line 1794
GIVEN c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income deemed to be from a business or profession under section 47A(b1) for` c MEANS
    `for tax year` (c's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (IF   c's `tax year` AT LEAST 2025
         THEN 52% TIMES max 0 (c's `refund received in the tax year of contributions overpaid in an earlier year, without any addition under section 362` MINUS `s 47A — the contributions paid, less the s 179(a) addition, for` c)
         ELSE 0)

@ref ITO s 47A(a), (b1), lines 1792-1794; fork F9a
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the cap of section 47A(a) in subsection (b1)`
      c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47A(a), (b), (b1) — the deduction, reading the cap in (b1) as` r `, for` c MEANS
    IF   NOT `(b1) applies`
    THEN min `before the cap` `the cap`
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `the cap of subsection (a) applies`          THEN min `before the cap` `the cap`
         WHEN `the cap of subsection (a) does not apply`   THEN `before the cap`
         WHEN `declined where the cap decides`
             THEN IF   `before the cap` AT MOST `the cap`
                  THEN `before the cap`
                  ELSE `section 47A(b1) does not say whether the cap of subsection (a) on the deduction survives it, and here the cap decides`
    WHERE
        `before the cap` MEANS `s 47A — the deduction before any cap, for` c
        `the cap`        MEANS max 0 (c's `taxable income before the deduction`)
        `(b1) applies`   MEANS c's `tax year` AT LEAST 2025 AND c's `refund received in the tax year of contributions overpaid in an earlier year, without any addition under section 362` GREATER THAN 0

-- (c) and (d): medical insurance for one exempt from parallel tax.
@ref ITO s 47A(c), (d), lines 1795, 1797; fork F9
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 47A(c) after 1996`
      c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47A(c) — the deduction for medical insurance, reading the survival of (c) as` r `, for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `sums paid in the tax year for medical insurance, other than dental, to a body the Minister of Finance determined` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `subsection (c) lapses with the Parallel Tax Law` THEN 0
         WHEN `subsection (c) survives` THEN `section 47A(c) caps the deduction at the parallel tax that would have applied, and the Parallel Tax Law applies to no tax year after 1996, so the text gives no cap`
         WHEN `declined where medical insurance sums were paid` THEN `section 47A(c) does not say whether it survives subsection (d) for a tax year after 1996, and here medical insurance sums were paid`

@ref ITO s 47A, lines 1792-1797; forks F9, F9a
GIVEN rb IS A `A reading of the cap of section 47A(a) in subsection (b1)`
      rc IS A `A reading of section 47A(c) after 1996`
      c  IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` rb `and subsection (c) as` rc `, for` c MEANS
    `for tax year` (c's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (`s 47A(a), (b), (b1) — the deduction, reading the cap in (b1) as` rb `, for` c PLUS `s 47A(c) — the deduction for medical insurance, reading the survival of (c) as` rc `, for` c)

@export The deduction under Income Tax Ordinance s 47A, in NIS, for a tax year from 2024: 52% of the National Insurance contributions paid on income that is not work income (and on work income by one whose employer is not liable), less the s 179(a) addition, up to the taxable income before the deduction; from 2025 less a refund received; declines where (b1) leaves the cap uncertain and where medical insurance sums were paid (s 47A(c))
@ref ITO s 47A, lines 1791-1797
GIVEN c IS A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
          @desc the tax year, the contributions paid on income that is not work income and on work income by one whose employer is not liable, the s 179(a) addition they include, any refund received, the taxable income before the deduction, and any medical insurance sums
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47A for` c MEANS
    `the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` `section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of the cap in subsection (b1)` `and subsection (c) as` `section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of subsection (c)` `, for` c
